  "kanji": "寺",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 寺\ntitle: Buddhist temple\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-2, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 6\nradical: 寸\nradicalNumber: 41\nonyomi: [ジ]\nkunyomi: [てら]\ndistractors: [時, 待, 持]\n---\n\n# 寺 — Buddhist temple\n\n**Strokes:** 6 · **Key (radical):** 寸 (no. 41) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n寺 てら names a Buddhist temple. The on reading ジ occurs in 古寺 こじ, old temple, and 寺社 じしゃ, temples and shrines. These words do not make temple and shrine interchangeable categories.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** See a 土-like upper shape over 寸 and imagine a small temple model resting on a hand. The scene is invented from the modern shape; it is not a claim about the historical role of either component.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ジ | on | 古寺 こじ - old temple |\n| てら | kun | [寺](../words/寺.md) てら - Buddhist temple |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [寺](../words/寺.md) てら - Buddhist temple\n- 古寺 こじ - old temple\n- 寺社 じしゃ - temples and shrines\n- [寺院](../words/寺院.md) じいん - temple; religious building\n\n## Notes\n\n- Do not read the standalone word for temple じ merely because temple names can end in that reading. Learn the reading of each name separately.\n- Compare [時](時.md), time, [待](待.md), wait, and [持](持.md), hold. Each adds a different left-hand component to the visible 寺 shape.\n- The indexing radical is 寸, not the upper 土-like shape.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1315240, 1315250, 1578440, 1635210.\n",
